  {/* TODO: add a Claresholm-specific detail from a real job (what was done, house type) once the owner confirms */}
  <p>Claresholm is about an hour's drive from our base in Lethbridge, up Highway 2. We've completed roofing jobs there, and we're happy to make the trip. You get the same thing a Lethbridge homeowner gets: a free inspection, a detailed written quote, and our Yard-Clean Promise when the job is done.</p>

  <h2>Built for Highway 2 wind</h2>
  <p>Anyone who's lived in Claresholm knows the wind. With the Porcupine Hills to the west and open prairie all around, Chinook gusts come through hard, and older shingle roofs pay for it. Lifted tabs, broken seal strips and shingles in the ditch after a big blow are common.</p>
  <p>For most Claresholm homes, we recommend <a href="/architectural-shingles/">architectural laminate shingles</a> — heavier, better sealed and rated for much higher wind speeds than 3-tab. <a href="/metal-roofing-lethbridge/">Metal roofing</a> is also worth pricing if you're planning to stay long-term, especially on garages, shops and acreage buildings.</p>

